{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012fMp1GYtCLhVFjesBMnJsH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nLooking at the task, I need to verify that the existing `BuildBinary` implementation in `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` already satisfies the requirements. Let me review what's already there against the requirements.\n\nFrom the source code provided (lines 277-290):\n\n```go\nfunc BuildBinary(t *testing.T, dir string) string {\n    t.Helper()\n    out := filepath.Join(t.TempDir(), \"binary\")\n    cmd := exec.Command(\"go\", \"build\", \"-o\", out, dir)\n    var stderr bytes.Buffer\n    cmd.Stderr = &stderr\n    if err := cmd.Run(); err != nil {\n        t.Fatalf(\"BuildBinary: go build %s: %v\\n%s\", dir, err, stderr.String())\n    }\n    return out\n}\n```\n\nChecking against the requirements:\n- **R1**: BuildBinary compiles Go package at dir and returns path - **done**\n- **R2**: Uses t.TempDir() for output location - **done**\n- **R3**: Calls t.Fatal (via t.Fatalf) with build output on failure - **done**\n- **R4**: Binary name derived from package directory name - **NOT done**. Currently uses hardcoded `\"binary\"` instead of deriving from dir.\n\nAlso checking design decisions:\n- **D1**: Uses `exec.Command(\"go\", \"build\", \"-o\", outputPath, dir)` - **done**\n- **D2**: Output path should be `filepath.Join(t.TempDir(), basename)` where basename is last element of dir - **NOT done**\n- **D3**: Works from within Go module with relative paths like `\".\"` - **done** (but with `\".\"` the basename would be `\".\"` which is wrong)\n\nI need to fix the binary name derivation. For `\".\"`, I should resolve to the actual directory name. Let me also check what `filepath.Base(\".\")` returns — it returns `\".\"`, which isn't useful. I need to handle that case.\n\nLet me read the SRD for exact requirements."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creatio